    "category": "Marketplace",
    "content": "\n      <p>Nigeria has one of Africa's largest and most active e-commerce markets. With over 100 million internet users and a booming entrepreneurial culture, Nigerians are buying and selling online more than ever before. Whether you're a buyer looking for the best deals or a seller wanting to reach millions of customers, this guide covers the best online marketplaces in Nigeria in 2026.</p>\n\n      <h2>1. Jumia Nigeria</h2>\n      <p>Jumia is Nigeria's largest e-commerce platform and one of the biggest in Africa. It operates like Amazon, allowing both businesses and individuals to sell products across a wide range of categories.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Best for:</strong> Electronics, fashion, home appliances, beauty products</li>\n        <li><strong>Fees:</strong> Commission-based — 3–15% per sale depending on category</li>\n        <li><strong>Delivery:</strong> Nationwide delivery across Nigeria</li>\n        <li><strong>Payment:</strong> Card, bank transfer, Jumia Pay, cash on delivery</li>\n        <li><strong>Best for buyers:</strong> Wide selection, frequent flash sales and discounts</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>2. Konga</h2>\n      <p>Konga is one of Nigeria's oldest and most trusted e-commerce platforms. It offers a marketplace for third-party sellers alongside its own retail inventory.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Best for:</strong> Electronics, phones, fashion, groceries</li>\n        <li><strong>Fees:</strong> Monthly seller subscription plus commission</li>\n        <li><strong>Delivery:</strong> Available in major Nigerian cities</li>\n        <li><strong>Payment:</strong> KongaPay, card, bank transfer</li>\n        <li><strong>Best feature:</strong> Strong buyer protection and return policy</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>3. Jiji Nigeria</h2>\n      <p>Jiji is Nigeria's most popular classified ads platform — think of it as Nigeria's version of Craigslist but much more active. It's completely free to list and is extremely popular for second-hand goods.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Best for:</strong> Second hand phones, cars, furniture, electronics, property</li>\n        <li><strong>Fees:</strong> Free basic listing, paid promotions available</li>\n        <li><strong>Delivery:</strong> Buyer and seller arrange directly</li>\n        <li><strong>Payment:</strong> Direct between buyer and seller</li>\n        <li><strong>Best feature:</strong> Huge volume of listings, free to use</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>4. Facebook Marketplace Nigeria</h2>\n      <p>Facebook Marketplace has become one of the most active buying and selling platforms in Nigeria. With nearly every Nigerian on Facebook, it offers unmatched reach especially for local buyers and sellers.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Best for:</strong> Local buying and selling, furniture, phones, fashion, food</li>\n        <li><strong>Fees:</strong> Completely free</li>\n        <li><strong>Delivery:</strong> Arranged directly between buyer and seller</li>\n        <li><strong>Payment:</strong> Direct between buyer and seller</li>\n        <li><strong>Best feature:</strong> Massive user base, easy to use, integrated with Facebook groups</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>5. Makola Digital</h2>\n      <p>Makola Digital is Africa's growing marketplace connecting buyers and sellers across Nigeria, Ghana and the wider African diaspora. It's completely free to list and is rapidly expanding across West Africa.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Best for:</strong> Products, services, jobs, rentals — all categories</li>\n        <li><strong>Fees:</strong> Completely free to list — no commission, no hidden fees</li>\n        <li><strong>Delivery:</strong> Arranged directly between buyer and seller</li>\n        <li><strong>Payment:</strong> Direct between buyer and seller</li>\n        <li><strong>Best feature:</strong> Free listing, WhatsApp integration, reaches buyers in Ghana and the diaspora</li>\n        <li><strong>Perfect for:</strong> Nigerian sellers wanting to reach Ghanaian buyers and the African diaspora in UK, USA and Canada</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>Nigerian sellers on Makola Digital can reach buyers across Ghana, UK, USA and Canada — making it perfect for cross-border trade within West Africa and the diaspora.</p>\n\n      <h2>6. Tonaton Nigeria</h2>\n      <p>Tonaton is a popular classified ads platform operating across West Africa including Nigeria and Ghana. It's free to use and popular for vehicles, property and electronics.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Best for:</strong> Cars, property, electronics, jobs</li>\n        <li><strong>Fees:</strong> Free basic listing</li>\n        <li><strong>Delivery:</strong> Arranged directly</li>\n        <li><strong>Best feature:</strong> Strong in both Nigeria and Ghana — great for cross-border sellers</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>7. Instagram & WhatsApp</h2>\n      <p>Many Nigerian businesses and individuals sell directly through Instagram and WhatsApp without using any formal marketplace. This is especially common in fashion, beauty, food and handmade products.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Best for:</strong> Fashion, beauty, food, handmade items, digital products</li>\n        <li><strong>Fees:</strong> Free</li>\n        <li><strong>Best feature:</strong> Direct relationship with customers, no platform commission</li>\n        <li><strong>Challenge:</strong> Building an audience takes time and consistency</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>8. Paystack Storefront</h2>\n      <p>Paystack — owned by Stripe — offers Nigerian businesses a free storefront to sell products and collect payments online. It's simple to set up and integrates Nigerian payment methods seamlessly.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Best for:</strong> Small businesses wanting their own online store</li>\n        <li><strong>Fees:</strong> 1.5% + NGN 100 per transaction (capped at NGN 2,000)</li>\n        <li><strong>Payment:</strong> Card, bank transfer, USSD, mobile money</li>\n        <li><strong>Best feature:</strong> Easy setup, trusted Nigerian payment processor</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>Tips for Selling Online Successfully in Nigeria</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Use multiple platforms</strong> — list on Jiji, Facebook Marketplace AND Makola Digital to maximise your reach</li>\n        <li><strong>Take great photos</strong> — clear, well-lit photos get significantly more inquiries</li>\n        <li><strong>Respond quickly</strong> — Nigerian buyers often message multiple sellers at once</li>\n        <li><strong>Be specific in your description</strong> — include brand, size, colour, condition and location</li>\n        <li><strong>Use WhatsApp</strong> — most Nigerian buyers prefer to communicate via WhatsApp</li>\n        <li><strong>Price competitively</strong> — research what similar items sell for before listing</li>\n        <li><strong>Build trust</strong> — respond professionally and deliver on your promises</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>Start Selling on Makola Digital Today</h2>\n      <p>Makola Digital is completely free for Nigerian sellers. List your products, services, jobs or rentals and reach buyers across Nigeria, Ghana, UK, USA and Canada. No commission, no hidden fees — just free exposure to buyers across West Africa and the diaspora.</p>\n    "
